Drop target for the packaged face library (docs/FACE_GENERATION_PLAN.md §7).

    python3 tools/faces/package_faces.py
    cp tools/faces/out/Faces/*.heic          dynasty/dynasty/Resources/Faces/
    cp tools/faces/out/faces_manifest.json   dynasty/dynasty/Resources/Faces/

The Xcode project is a filesystem-synchronized root group, so anything added
here is bundled on the next build with no project-file edit. Measured: the
sync FLATTENS subdirectories, so the files land at the bundle ROOT
(dynasty.app/face_00000.heic, dynasty.app/faces_manifest.json) — which is why
FaceImageCache.bundleURL and FaceLibrary.loadManifest each try the bundle root
as well as the "Faces" subdirectory.

This directory is intentionally empty: the app renders a placeholder
silhouette for every missing image, and shipping a PARTIAL faces_manifest.json
would be worse than none (the manifest is authoritative when present, so it
would shrink the catalog to whatever ids it lists).

After dropping the files, verify the build actually picked them up — do not
eyeball the .app:

    SIMCTL_CHILD_FACE_BUNDLE_AUDIT=1 xcrun simctl launch --console-pty \
      <device> com.brewcrow.dynasty | grep FACEBUNDLE

Expect `catalog=manifest/<n>` and `images resolved=n/n`. A FAIL means the
manifest did not decode (the app silently falls back to the synthesized
catalog) or images shipped that the manifest does not list.
